@startuml architecture
title EAP-DID: Entities and Interfaces\nFigure 1

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica

rectangle "Peer System" #E8F5E9 {
    component "EAP Peer\n(wpa_supplicant,\nEAP-DID method)" as wpa
    artifact "Credential Store\nVC (JWT), subject\nsecp256k1 key,\nX25519 key, did:peer" as cred
}

rectangle "Access Network" #E3F2FD {
    component "Authenticator\n(IEEE 802.1X PAE)" as ap
    component "EAP Server\n(hostapd,\nEAP-DID method)" as radius
}

rectangle "Relying Infrastructure" #FFF3E0 {
    component "Verifier\n(DIDComm endpoint,\nVP validation)" as verifier
    component "Key Service\n<i>non-normative</i>\n<i>test deployment only</i>" as keysvc
}

database "Verifiable Data\nRegistry (VDR)\nIssuer DIDs,\nstatus lists" as ledger #FFEBEE

rectangle "Issuing Authority\n(enrolment phase only)" #F3E5F5 {
    component "Issuer\n(VC issuance)" as issuer
}

wpa <-right-> ap : EAPOL [802.1X]\nEAP [RFC3748], Method Type 57
ap -right-> radius : RADIUS [RFC2865]\nEAP-Message AVP
radius -right-> verifier : presentation request;\nVP relay; status poll
radius --> keysvc : recipient key retrieval
keysvc --> verifier : key store read
verifier --> ledger : issuer DID resolution;\ncredential status

cred .up.> wpa : provisioned out of band
issuer .up.> cred : VC issuance [DIDComm v2]
issuer .right.> ledger : DID publication

cred -[hidden]down- issuer

note bottom of radius
  <b>Key derivation (EAP server)</b>
  MSK, EMSK per [RFC5247] are derived from the
  JWE Content Encryption Key (CEK) recovered by
  unwrapping the Verifier recipient entry.
  See Figure 3, Section 6.
end note

note bottom of wpa
  <b>Key derivation (EAP peer)</b>
  The peer generates the CEK when constructing the
  JWE and retains it. No Holder agent participates
  in the authentication exchange.
end note

note right of keysvc
  <b>Non-normative component.</b>
  Discloses private key material. Present only
  because the EAP server and the Verifier are
  distinct processes in this deployment. It is
  removed when the EAP server performs VP
  validation locally.
end note

legend bottom
  <b>Trust model</b>: Model D of eap-did-models.md.
  The Issuer DID is the only identifier published to the VDR.
  The Peer identifier is a did:prism long form; the Verifier
  identifier is a did:peer minted per exchange.
  --
  Solid: authentication exchange, per association.
  Dashed: enrolment, performed once.
  The Issuer is not contacted during authentication.
endlegend

@enduml
